  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Emergency Response to Sheltered Families with Children and Adolescents Victims of the Floods in Rio Grande do Sul State in Brazil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address the urgent needs of families with children and adolescents affected by extreme climatic events in the state of Rio Grande do Sul, particularly those in shelters. The project focuses on documentation assistance, provision of information about child rights, and the Prevention of Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (PSEA). Institutional beneficiaries include government entities such as Child Protection Services, documentation authorities, social services, welfare departments and local disaster response agencies, as well as non-governmental organizations and community-based organizations focused on child welfare, legal support and PSEA. These entities are receiving capacity-building training on children&apos;s rights in the context of mobility and disasters. The training aims to ensure the best interests of the child by raising awareness about participation, protection, safety, access to rights and non-discrimination.</narrative>
  </description>
